   "says": "Most consonants can represent both \"soft\" (palatalized, represented in the IPA with a ⟨ʲ⟩) and \"hard\" consonant phonemes. If consonant letters are followed by vowel letters, the soft/hard quality of the consonant depends on whether the vowel is meant to follow \"hard\" consonants ⟨а, о, э, у, ы⟩ or \"soft\" consonants ⟨я, ё, е, ю, и⟩. A soft sign ⟨ь⟩ indicates palatalization of the preceding consonant without adding a vowel.",
   "heads": [
    "after a hard consonant",
    "after a soft consonant"
   ],
