   "kind": "Russian letter",
   "name": "мягкий знак, the soft sign",
   "src": "alphabet",
   "says": "The soft sign, ⟨ь⟩, in most positions acts like a \"silent front vowel\" and indicates that the preceding consonant is palatalized (except for always-hard ж, ш, ц) and the following vowel (if present) is iotated […]. This is important as palatalization is phonemic in Russian. For example, брат [brat] ('brother') contrasts with брать [bratʲ] ('to take').",
